Z||000002||mrfiero||12-30-2001||02:39 PM||||A code 32 is rarely anything other than a vacuum leak.  Inspect all of the plastic and rubber lines that deal with the EGR system.<P>The most likely culprit is the rubber hose that runs from the EGR solenoid to the firewall.  Over time this hose deteriorates and cracks or just falls off completely.<P>The EGR solenoid is the black cylindrical looking thing on the passenger side of the engine (below the thermostat housing). <P>In some rare cases (never has happened to me) the EGR solenoid itself goes bad and trips the code.<P>Check the hoses and lines first though, then go from there.   <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 12-30-2001).]||||reg||1
